                <pb facs="0881" n="869" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg869"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.85/175: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-05-10T21:00:00-04:00">May 10, 1943—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 11—1:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>874. My 854, May 8.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d830-f1"/> Vial came Embassy tonight
                    urging completion sales contract at once, inspection tests, et cetera to follow.
                    Vial <pb facs="0882" n="870" xml:id="pg870"/> states popular hostile attitude
                    developing here and company anxious to publish statement to clarify to public.
                    He appeared surprised when informed German radio made reference to sale. Embassy
                    impressed Vial now much concerned lest sale fall through. Opinion Vial my 829,
                    May 5.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
